fuckwayland for Arch
====================

Nothing is on the AUR yet -- publishing there is the owner's call, not a
licence problem any more: the tree is BSD-2-Clause since HEAD 375d815, the
recipe says `license=('BSD-2-Clause')` and package() installs the text under
/usr/share/licenses/fuckwayland/.  Today the route is: clone, build, install
your own build.

  sh scripts/build-pkgbuild.sh       # -> dist/fuckwayland-<ver>-1-any.pkg.tar.zst
  sudo pacman -U ./dist/fuckwayland-*.pkg.tar.zst

`--no-deps` fails instead of installing build tools, `--lint` runs namcap on
the recipe and on the package, `--keep` leaves the scratch build directory
under dist/, and `--help` prints the header of the script.  makepkg refuses to
run as root, so in a container do it as an ordinary user.

The script writes PKGBUILD.local into dist/pkgbuild/, never beside
packaging/arch/PKGBUILD, so a build leaves `git status` nothing to explain.
Same recipe, with `source=("fuckwayland-<ver>.tar.gz")` pointing at the tarball
`git archive` just made and its real sha256.  Nothing in what is built is SKIP.

Arch is the best oracle this project has
----------------------------------------

`extra` carries xdotool 4.20260303.1, wmctrl 1.07, xorg-xprop 1.2.8 and
xorg-xrandr 1.5.4 -- the exact four versions these tools clone byte for byte.
Ubuntu 24.04 and 26.04 ship xdotool 3.20160805.1, which is why README's
footnote (b) has to explain that the X11 handover lands on a tool without
`windowstate`.  On Arch it lands on the oracle itself.  (Measured in an Arch
bootstrap root: `xprop -root` and `wxprop -root` were byte-identical over a
live X server, and `warandr --command` drove Arch's own xrandr.)

wl-mirror is in `extra` too, not a third-party repo, and `acl` is in `core`
and pulled in by systemd -- so `setfacl` is always there and the removal
scriptlet's python fallback never runs on Arch.  It is kept because one
procedure serves three packagings.

What differs from the .deb
--------------------------

  * Python lands in /usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages, which is versioned, so
    there is no "one package for both releases" story here: a python minor
    bump wants a pkgrel rebuild.  A built .pkg.tar.zst is a CI artifact and is
    never committed to this repository.
  * The .pyc files ship in the package (134 of them, written by `python -m
    installer`), where dpkg compiles them on your machine at configure time.
  * /etc/xdg/autostart/fuckwayland-enable-bridge.desktop is a plain file.
    pacman has no conffiles -- only backup=() entries are preserved -- so it
    goes in and comes out again with the package, and the .deb's symlink
    round the conffile rule has no reason to exist here.
  * `arch=('any')` holds only because build() regenerates the overlap
    extension's three type descriptions with gobject-introspection; the
    checked-in ones are LP64 blobs.  See the comment on the `arch=` line.
  * The install hints name Arch's packages: `pacman -S xorg-xprop`,
    `xorg-xrandr`, `python-gobject gtk3`.  fwcommon/distro.py is the table,
    and tests/test_packaging_names.py keeps it and this recipe's optdepends
    saying the same thing.

/dev/uinput
-----------

The rule tags the node `uaccess` and systemd-logind gives the user at the
active seat an ACL on it at every login.  post_install applies it to the
running system too, so no reboot is needed.  pacman's own
35-systemd-udev-reload hook also reloads the rules, but it runs after the
scriptlet -- which is why the scriptlet reloads before it triggers, and why
the order is what the tests pin.

`pacman -R fuckwayland` puts the node back to root:root 0600 with no ACL and
takes /var/lib/fuckwayland with it (measured).

Anyone who can open /dev/uinput can type as you.  The threat model is in
README.md.

The bridge, and the one re-login
--------------------------------

Identical to the .deb: gnome-shell scans extension directories only at login,
enabling an extension is a per-user dconf setting, and pacman runs as root.
The extension is installed system-wide and enabled in each user's first GNOME
session by /etc/xdg/autostart/fuckwayland-enable-bridge.desktop.  Install, log
out, log back in.

